Jest globals are not injected in ESM mode? In ESM, `jest` object is not globally available by default? Actually with ESM, `jest` global might not be defined unless `injectGlobals`; describe/it/expect are injected though apparently because tests ran. `jest` object specific maybe available via `import { jest } from "@jest/globals"`. But @jest/globals resolution: node_modules doesn't have @jest/globals? Check. Or use `globalThis.jest`? Better avoid jest mocks: manually spy on console.log by replacing and restoring. That's framework agnostic and works.

Use:
```
const originalLog = console.log;
beforeEach(() => { console.log = (...args)=>{ logs.push(args); }; });
afterEach(() => { console.log = originalLog; ...});
```
But parallel test files in same process? Jest runs each test file in separate environment (vm), console maybe isolated. Fine.

Within each describe, define `let logs; const originalLog = console.log;` at module level? beforeEach sets. We need restore even if test fails. afterEach.

Implement helper:
```
let logs, originalLog;
beforeEach(() => { logs=[]; originalLog=console.log; console.log=(...args)=>{logs.push(args);}; });
afterEach(() => { console.log=originalLog; ...});
```
Careful originalLog assignment each beforeEach to current console.log; if previous restore happened okay. Better keep module-level `const realLog = console.log;` and restore to realLog. Since tests in same file run sequentially. Use module-level.

Then logging test uses `logs`.

Note first describe defines its own beforeEach and logSpy; replace too.

Let's patch.

